. * ============================
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3
. * ============================
. 
. * To empirically test this hypothesis, we use a fixed-effects regression mode
> l. The dependent variable (fem_unpaid_labor_share) represents the share of un
> paid household labor performed by female household members, calculated as the
>  proportion of total household unpaid labor hours contributed by women.
. 
. * The main independent variable of interest is a binary indicator (d_daughter
> ) indicating whether the household includes at least one daughter (1) or none
>  (0). The regression controls for household income, the age difference betwee
> n male and female household members, average household age, average household
>  education, the educational difference between male and female household memb
> ers, migration background, and interactions between region and survey year to
>  account for regional and temporal variation. Standard errors are clustered a
> t the household level to account for within-household correlations.
. 
. xtset hid syear

